\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Study design and observation boundary. Addition and subtraction modulo 97 are evaluated under a shared fixed-rate MLP protocol crossing three hidden widths, two weight-decay settings, and three initialization seeds. Memorization requires training accuracy of at least 99\%; generalization requires held-out accuracy of at least 95\%, each for three consecutive checkpoints. Non-attainment at 20,000 updates is not a measured generalization delay. The diagram summarizes the design, not a proposed neural circuit.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{Study design and observation boundary. Addition and subtraction modulo 97 are evaluated under a shared fixed-rate MLP protocol crossing three hidden widths, two weight-decay settings, and three initialization seeds. Memorization requires training accuracy of at least 99\%; generalization requires held-out accuracy of at least 95\%, each for three consecutive checkpoints. Non-attainment at 20,000 updates is not a measured generalization delay. The diagram summarizes the design, not a proposed neural circuit}{figure.caption.1}{}}
