\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Administrative endpoint substitution determines the displayed lag. Circles denote addition and squares subtraction; horizontal bars are condition means. Filled symbols indicate observed memorization; hollow symbols indicate memorization non-attainment. All generalization events are unobserved. The focused vertical range does not begin at zero. In panel (a), earlier fitting at larger widths increases $H-T_{\mathrm  {M}}$. In panel (b), the hollow width-16 observations instead receive the special value $H$, creating a positive narrow-minus-wide contrast without any observed generalization event.}}{7}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:censoring}{{3}{7}{Administrative endpoint substitution determines the displayed lag. Circles denote addition and squares subtraction; horizontal bars are condition means. Filled symbols indicate observed memorization; hollow symbols indicate memorization non-attainment. All generalization events are unobserved. The focused vertical range does not begin at zero. In panel (a), earlier fitting at larger widths increases $H-\TM $. In panel (b), the hollow width-16 observations instead receive the special value $H$, creating a positive narrow-minus-wide contrast without any observed generalization event}{figure.caption.7}{}}
